        "body": "RECOMMENDATION  |  Approve a diversified 24-month portfolio: 50% river interception, 32.5% ghost gear, 17.5% coastal reuse hubs.'"\\n\\nMODELED OUTCOME  |  1,330–2,270 tonnes removed or leakage avoided. Ranges are planning estimates—not commitments—and impact types are not perfectly additive.\\n\\nBOARD QUESTION  |  Is this the right balance of scalable prevention, direct ecological benefit, and community durability?\"
      }
    },
    {
      \"alias\": \"program_river\",
      \"recipe\": {
        \"kind\": \"native_card\",
        \"title\": \"01 • RIVER INTERCEPTION + CITY WASTE PARTNERS\",
        \"body\": \"ROLE  |  Stop plastic before it reaches the ocean; pair interception with local collection and disposal capacity.\\n\\n24-MONTH IMPACT  |  900–1,500 t leakage avoided\\nUNIT COST  |  "'$670–$1,110 per modeled tonne'"\\nEXECUTION RISK  |  MED–HIGH\\n\\nWHY CREDIBLE  |  Proven equipment category and measurable capture volumes.\\nWATCH  |  Permits, flood resilience, maintenance uptime, and verified downstream handling.\"
      }
    },
    {
      \"alias\": \"program_gear\",
      \"recipe\": {
        \"kind\": \"native_card\",
        \"title\": \"02 • GHOST GEAR RECOVERY + PREVENTION\",
        \"body\": \"ROLE  |  Remove abandoned fishing gear and prevent recurrence through port reception, tagging, and fisher incentives.\\n\\n24-MONTH IMPACT  |  250–450 t removed or avoided\\nUNIT COST  |  "'$1,440–$2,600 per modeled tonne'"\\nEXECUTION RISK  |  MEDIUM\\n\\nWHY CREDIBLE  |  Visible removals plus strong wildlife and habitat benefit.\\nWATCH  |  Retrieval safety, seasonal access, gear ownership, and double-counting prevention.\"
      }
    },
    {
      \"alias\": \"program_hubs\",
      \"recipe\": {
        \"kind\": \"native_card\",
        \"title\": \"03 • COASTAL REUSE + COLLECTION HUBS\",
        \"body\": \"ROLE  |  Build community-run collection, sorting, reuse, and verified end-market capacity in leakage hotspots.\\n\\n24-MONTH IMPACT  |  180–320 t collected or reused\\nUNIT COST  |  "'$1,090–$1,940 per modeled tonne'"\\nEXECUTION RISK  |  MED–HIGH\\n\\nWHY CREDIBLE  |  Durable local capacity and livelihoods; adaptable to multiple waste streams.\\nWATCH  |  End-market demand, price volatility, worker safeguards, and additionality.\"
      }
    },
    {
      \"alias\": \"fund_river\",
      \"recipe\": {
        \"kind\": \"native_card\",
        \"title\": \""'$1,000,000 • 50% • RIVER",
        "body": "FUND  |  1–2 sites with equipment, two-year operations, local waste-system integration, and independent measurement.'"\\n\\nRATIONALE  |  Largest allocation to the strongest prevention economics and highest scale potential.\\n\\nTRANCHES  |  40% contract • 40% operational milestone • 20% verified performance.\"
      }
    },
    {
      \"alias\": \"fund_gear\",
      \"recipe\": {
        \"kind\": \"native_card\",
        \"title\": \""'$650,000 • 32.5% • GHOST GEAR",
        "body": "FUND  |  Priority retrieval zones plus port reception, gear marking, and fisher-return incentives.'"\\n\\nRATIONALE  |  Accept a higher unit cost for direct wildlife, navigation, and habitat benefit.\\n\\nTRANCHES  |  40% mobilization • 40% verified retrieval • 20% prevention adoption.\"
      }
    },
    {
      \"alias\": \"fund_hubs\",
      \"recipe\": {
        \"kind\": \"native_card\",
        \"title\": \""'$350,000 • 17.5% • COASTAL HUBS",
        "body": "FUND  |  3–5 small pilots with local operators, worker safeguards, buyer agreements, and reusable packaging trials.'"\\n\\nRATIONALE  |  Keep this a disciplined option bet until end-market durability is demonstrated.\\n\\nTRANCHES  |  40% setup • 40% throughput • 20% verified sales or reuse.\"
      }
    },
    {
      \"alias\": \"rule_stage\",
      \"recipe\": {
        \"kind\": \"native_card\",
        \"title\": \"RULE 1 • RELEASE MONEY IN STAGES\",
        \"body\": \"Use 40 / 40 / 20 tranches for every award.\\n\\nRelease the final 20% only after independent evidence of volume, cost, legal disposal or reuse, and no material safety breach.\\n\\nNo verified evidence = no release.\"
      }
    },
    {
      \"alias\": \"rule_reallocate\",
      \"recipe\": {
        \"kind\": \"native_card\",
        \"title\": \"RULE 2 • REALLOCATE EARLY\",
        \"body\": \"If a program misses two consecutive quarterly thresholds, shift up to 15% of its unspent balance to the strongest performer.\\n\\nRequire board-chair + program-chair approval and a written additionality check.\"
      }
    },
    {
      \"alias\": \"rule_stop_scale\",
      \"recipe\": {
        \"kind\": \"native_card\",
        \"title\": \"RULE 3 • STOP / HOLD / SCALE\",
        \"body\": \"STOP  |  Verified cost exceeds "'$3,000/t, disposal is untraceable, or safety fails.'"\\nHOLD  |  Permits, buyers, or local ownership are unresolved.\\nSCALE  |  Cost is ≤"'$1,500/t and an audit confirms ≥80% of claimed volume, with a credible next-site pipeline."
      }
    },
    {
      "alias": "week_owner",
      "recipe": {
        "kind": "native_card",
        "title": "WEEK 1 • ACTION 1 • NAME THE OWNER",
        "body": "By Day 2, appoint one portfolio lead and approve a one-page measurement charter.'"\\n\\nDefine: tonne basis, avoided-vs-removed labels, baseline, additionality, audit method, safety, and quarterly dashboard owner.\"
      }
    },
    {
      \"alias\": \"week_diligence\",
      \"recipe\": {
        \"kind\": \"native_card\",
        \"title\": \"WEEK 1 • ACTION 2 • OPEN DILIGENCE\",
        \"body\": \"By Day 3, launch a 10-day diligence sprint with two candidates per program.\\n\\nVerify operators, sites, permits, maintenance, unit economics, local consent, worker safeguards, downstream traceability, and references.\"
      }
    },
    {
      \"alias\": \"week_terms\",
      \"recipe\": {
        \"kind\": \"native_card\",
        \"title\": \"WEEK 1 • ACTION 3 • ISSUE TERM SHEETS\",
        \"body\": \"By Day 5, send conditional term sheets using the 40 / 40 / 20 structure.\\n\\nInclude audit rights, quarterly thresholds, stop/reallocation clauses, data ownership, incident reporting, and a 30-day contracting deadline.\"
